  "verbalization": "Deferiprone is associated with Dominant Beta-thalassemia through a chain of indications involving Luspatercept. The evidence suggests that Deferiprone is used to treat Beta-thalassemia Intermedia and Beta-thalassemia Hbb/lcrb, both of which are subtypes of Beta-thalassemia, and that Luspatercept, a drug targeting these conditions, is indicated for Dominant Beta-thalassemia. This creates a potential pathway where Deferiprone, through its indication on Beta-thalassemia subtypes, indirectly influences the treatment of Dominant Beta-thalassemia via Luspatercept. The shared use of Luspatercept in these contexts implies a possible mechanistic link, though the exact relationship remains unclear. The evidence supports a hypothesis that Deferiprone may contribute to the treatment of Dominant Beta-thalassemia through its role in influencing the pathophysiology of Beta-thalassemia subtypes, but further research is needed to clarify the precise mechanism.",
